post_install() {
    getent group wg-server >/dev/null || groupadd --system wg-server
    getent passwd wg-server >/dev/null || useradd --system --gid wg-server \
        --no-create-home --shell /usr/bin/nologin \
        --comment "wg-vpn server (apply)" wg-server
    chown root:wg-server /etc/wg-server
    chmod 750 /etc/wg-server
    # Re-apply on upgrade too: makepkg's install -dm750 only sets the
    # mode on first install, and an upgrade from a package version that
    # created this world-readable (0755) would otherwise keep that mode.
    chmod 750 /etc/wg-client

    cat <<'EOF'
==> wg-vpn installed. Next steps:
    Server: put your topology JSON (README.md "Configure") at
      /etc/wg-server/config.json, readable by the wg-server user, then:
        sudo systemctl enable --now wg-server.timer
    Client: put your client JSON at /etc/wg-client/config.json, then:
        sudo systemctl enable --now wg-client.timer
        sudo systemctl enable --now wg-client-boot.timer
    Enable BOTH client timers: wg-client.timer is the daily 00:30 UTC
    slot (randomized delay so a fleet doesn't hit the bucket at once, see
    wg-client.timer's RandomizedDelaySec); wg-client-boot.timer runs a
    sync pass shortly after boot with no jitter, so a reboot doesn't wait
    on that same randomized delay to restore the tunnel. wg-client
    reconciles a missing/down interface on that boot pass even when the
    on-disk config is unchanged.
    Do NOT also enable wg-quick@wg0 (or any other tunnel controller) for
    the same interface -- wg-client configures the kernel WireGuard
    device itself over netlink/UAPI, and a second controller managing the
    same interface would race it (docs/wg-client.md §3, §7, §8).
    Both timers/services also work with `systemctl start` for a one-off
    run, and `journalctl -u wg-server.service` / `-u wg-client.service`
    for logs.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}

post_remove() {
    getent passwd wg-server >/dev/null && userdel wg-server
    getent group wg-server >/dev/null && groupdel wg-server
    true
}
